<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines awards $200 mln deal to China's Harbin.</title>
<headline>Philippines awards $200 mln deal to China's Harbin.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-owned National Power Corp of the Philippines said on Thursday its board had approved a proposal of China's Harbin Power Engineering Co to construct a coal-fired power plant worth about $200 million in southern Philippines.  </p>
<p>The 200 megawatt power plant will be interconnected with the southern Mindanao grid, a Napocor statement said.</p>
<p>Harbin is undertaking the project with a local firm State Investment under a build-operate-transfer scheme, Napocor said.</p>
<p>The two firms will finance, construct the plant, and manage the fuel supplies for 25 years.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
